# Bundled FFmpeg — provided per platform at build time, never committed.
# Shipping one here only ever worked on the machine that produced it: the old
# bin/ffmpeg was an arm64 Mach-O stub dynamically linked against
# /opt/homebrew/Cellar/ffmpeg/7.1.1_1/, so it was useless on both Windows and
# any Mac without that exact Homebrew formula.
bin/ffmpeg
bin/ffmpeg.exe

# OS
Thumbs.db

# Node.js
node_modules/
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose. The frontend lockfile IS versioned — it
# pins the dependency tree the desktop bundle ships with, and gets refreshed on
# every release — so an unanchored pattern here contradicted a tracked file
# (gitignore never applies to files already in the index, so the rule silently
# did nothing for frontend/ while looking like it covered everything).
/package-lock.json

